@startuml fig_provenance_chain
' Signer-Independent Evaluation and Provenance Design
' UML 2.5 Component Diagram over the artefact chain.
' Verified against processed/splits/versions/*/split_metadata.json,
' backend/app/routers/training.py (_research_splits, _provenance_checks)
' and scripts/research_validity.py (evaluate_checkpoint, C1-C14).

skinparam defaultFontName "Times New Roman"
skinparam defaultFontSize 17
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam roundcorner 4
skinparam nodesep 55
skinparam ranksep 65
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam ArrowFontSize 14
skinparam ComponentBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #333333
skinparam ComponentFontSize 17
skinparam ArtifactBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ArtifactBorderColor #333333
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #333333
skinparam PackageBackgroundColor #FCFCFC
skinparam PackageBorderColor #777777
skinparam PackageFontSize 18
skinparam PackageFontStyle bold
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam NoteBorderColor #999999
skinparam NoteFontSize 14
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam LegendBorderColor #999999
skinparam LegendFontSize 14

package "Partitioning" as P1 {
  database "Sample corpus\nsamples, signers" as CORPUS
  component "Split generator" as GEN
  artifact "Versioned split directory\ntrain.csv / val.csv / test.csv" as SPLITDIR
  artifact "split_metadata.json\nsplit_mode, signer_disjoint,\nsigners per partition, counts,\nvalid_for_research" as META
}

package "Admission" as P2 {
  component "Gate 1 — Backend API\n_research_splits()" as G1
  component "Gate 2 — Trainer subprocess\n_enforce_research_preconditions()" as G2
}

package "Recorded provenance" as P3 {
  database "training_jobs.split_provenance\njsonb" as PROV
  artifact "Checkpoint contract fields\ndataset_version, split_version,\ndataset_manifest_checksum, git_commit,\nruntime environment, recognition_profile" as CONTRACT
}

package "On-demand assessment" as P4 {
  component "evaluate_checkpoint()\ncriteria C1 to C14" as EVAL
  artifact "Verdict\nvalid | invalid | undecidable" as VERDICT
}

CORPUS -down-> GEN
GEN -down-> SPLITDIR
GEN -down-> META

META -down-> G1
G1 -down-> G2
G2 -down-> PROV : freeze
G2 -down-> CONTRACT : stamp

PROV -down-> EVAL
CONTRACT -down-> EVAL
EVAL -down-> VERDICT

note right of META
  The generator writes train.csv, val.csv and test.csv over
  **disjoint sets of signers**, and records which signer went
  where. Disjointness covers the **validation** partition as well
  as the test partition, so model selection never sees a signer
  that is later used to report the result.
end note

note right of G1
  Gate 1 offers only flat, research-valid splits. LOSO and
  matched-leak fold sets are deliberately withheld: they are
  multi-run evaluation protocols, not a single training job.
  Splits flagged valid_for_research = false are withheld too,
  because Gate 2 would reject them anyway.
end note

note bottom of VERDICT
  Three-valued, fail-closed. A criterion that cannot be decided from the
  artefact yields **undecidable**, but only when no criterion has definitely
  failed; a definite failure always outranks an undecidable one.
end note

legend bottom
  What the fourteen criteria cover — C1 run intent (research, not the smoke_test default) | C2, C3 augmentation and
  checkpoint contract fields | C4, C5 dataset and split versioning plus manifest checksum | C6, C7, C12 split metadata
  present, research-valid, and a non-empty test set | C8, C9 recognition profile matches the labels, with no
  cross-profile leakage | C10, C11 runtime environment and git commit recorded | C13, C14 metrics taken from the
  restored best-validation checkpoint of a run that did not fail.
  The assessment is never run inside training: it reads the stored checkpoint only when a user asks for it, and its
  outcome is not written back to training_jobs.
endlegend

@enduml
